{
  "case_id": "2016-16-399",
  "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Whenever the Board rejects an employee's allegations that he was affected by an appealable civil service action, the Board is making a substantive decision on the merits of the employee's civil service claim. That point has nothing to do with the Board's jurisdiction and, therefore, nothing to do with whether the employee has brought a mixed case reviewable in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Christopher Landau",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: Well, you raise an interesting question, Your Honor, about exhaustion. Exhaustion is a defense. If the government -- if you're in the district court and the court rejects the -- the Board -- excuse me -- the court affirms the Board on the civil service claim -- again, that's really a merits determination that the Board has made, notwithstanding its label -- then there would certainly be a question, Your Honor, as to whether or not the discrimination case has been exhausted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So but -- by what -- what authority does a district court ever have the power to hear a civil service claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. Does that mean that a finding that this suspension or furlough wasn't of the required number of days, is that jurisdictional? Are you -- or are you just arguing that this situation involving a settlement agreement is not actually jurisdictional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Landau",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LANDAU: It is not -- when the Board decides -- if you -- as long as the complainant alleges something that is one of the serious civil service actions, if the -- if the Board rejects --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLETCHER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Federal Circuit generally has exclusive jurisdiction to review the MSPB's decisions. But Section 7703(b)(2) carves out an exception that sends mixed cases to the district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So again, on the tolling issue, I think either side is going to need some sort of tolling rule, and I think there's plenty of room to make that sort of tolling rule once it gets sorted out, which forum the employee --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We carve out mixed cases because those cases include claims of discrimination. Employees have a right to trial de novo on their discrimination claims, and you obviously can't get that in the Federal Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Then why --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I think the -- the rule that's at issue here -- and I just want to point out, even if you don't agree with me on this, that's not really the question presented in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Who wrote -- who wrote this statute? Somebody who --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you please tell me, besides this voluntary settlement issue, what else is jurisdictional? What else besides something that doesn't match 7512, the furlough and suspension?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Fletcher, when we're talking about folks knowing where to go and making it easier on them, can you help me with the same question I had for Mr. Landau? Which is (b)(2), as I read it, talks about cases of discrimination filed under Federal discrimination laws go to district court, and everything else goes to the Federal Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you think he has to ask that? Suppose he asked something else. Suppose he said, I'd like the district court just to decide this. Could he do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What happens if he went to the district court and said, I don't care about the Board deciding this issue, voluntary or not voluntary, I just want to pursue the -- the discrimination claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fletcher",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think if that's what he -- if that's what he wants, he should not seek review of the Board's decision at all, because the regulation that we talked about earlier, 1614.302(b) positions him. If he just acquiesces in the Board's decision to go exhaust his administrative -- his discrimination claim through the ordinary administrative process, through the agency EEO, and then through the EEOC, if he wants it. And then he can go straight to district court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So under your theory, the problem is that if you don't go to the MS -- if you don't go to the Federal Circuit, the district court, it will all get mucked up in the CSRA business because they can't go ahead and decide it, you have to wait, and it has to go back later because of Chenery issues and the like."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Landau",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the jurisdiction over a mixed question turns on the allegations and not just the outcome of the -- of the civil service action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-399",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0b19dc6f02344cf22158a13ad40d9bd24cf63f84e4f84b5da2cbb770a465865a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0b19dc6f0234-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
